---
// Rendered iterations of THE CONTESTED FOOTING (2026-08-11).
// Three geometries for the same content, on real crux data from the nuclear
// briefing. House rule: two or three rendered iterations before anything
// reader-facing ships. Noindex, unlinked, no ads.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="The Contested Footing (labs) - The Whetstone" noAds={true}>
  <Fragment slot="head"><meta name="robots" content="noindex" /></Fragment>
  <div class="fl">
<div class="wrap">
  <p class="kicker">The Whetstone · labs</p>
  <h1>The Contested Footing</h1>
  <p class="lede">Three ways to draw the same thing: the question, the premises the fight actually turns on, and what happened when each was checked. Real data from the nuclear costings briefing, not placeholder text.</p>
  <p class="note">There is no colour anywhere in any of these. The verdict is an English word in every instance; the geometry only repeats it. Print any of this in greyscale and nothing is lost. That is deliberate, and the evidence says it costs nothing: Dwyer, Hogan and Stewart tested monochrome argument maps against coloured ones with 400 undergraduates and the advantage held identically in both.</p>

  <hr class="rule">
  <h2>A. Beam and struts</h2>
  <p class="verdictline">The spec as written · diagram above, rows below</p>
  <p class="note">The beam is the axis and the thing being held up, one graphic doing two jobs. Each strut terminates in a way that pictures its verdict: solid to the baseline holds, stopping short is contested, dashed is never stated at all. The word underneath carries the meaning; the geometry is the reinforcement.</p>

  <p class="sizetag">Site width, 42rem</p>
  <div class="card site"><p class="eyebrow">The Whetstone · this question is mapped</p><p class="q">Is a nuclear pathway cheaper than a renewables-only one for Australia?</p><div class="poles"><span>← nuclear cheaper</span><span>renewables cheaper →</span></div><div class="beam"></div><div class="struts"><div class="strutcol" style="left:12.5%;transform:translateX(-50%)"><div class="strut unstated"></div></div><div class="strutcol" style="left:37.5%;transform:translateX(-50%)"><div class="strut contested"></div></div><div class="strutcol" style="left:62.5%;transform:translateX(-50%)"><div class="strut contested"></div></div><div class="strutcol" style="left:87.5%;transform:translateX(-50%)"><div class="strut unstated"></div></div></div><div class="baseline"></div><div class="words"><div class="wordcol" style="left:12.5%"><span class="word">UNSTATED</span><span class="ord">1</span></div><div class="wordcol" style="left:37.5%"><span class="word">CONTESTED</span><span class="ord">2</span></div><div class="wordcol" style="left:62.5%"><span class="word">CONTESTED</span><span class="ord">3</span></div><div class="wordcol" style="left:87.5%"><span class="word">UNSTATED</span><span class="ord">4</span></div></div><div class="rows"><div class="row"><span class="rnum">1</span><span class="rverdict">UNSTATED</span><span class="rtext">How often a reactor runs<span class="rfind"><span class="bang">! </span><b>Supplied.</b> Frontier needs 90 per cent uptime and never states it. GenCost prices 53 to 89 per cent, from coal’s own record.</span></span></div><div class="row"><span class="rnum">2</span><span class="rverdict">CONTESTED</span><span class="rtext">What the first plant costs<span class="rfind"><b>Factual.</b> Frontier removes the first-of-a-kind premium by the time nuclear is built. GenCost puts it above 100 per cent.</span></span></div><div class="row"><span class="rnum">3</span><span class="rverdict">CONTESTED</span><span class="rtext">How long the asset lives<span class="rfind"><b>Judgment call.</b> The same build cost spread over 50 years or recovered over 30. The choice is never argued for on either side.</span></span></div><div class="row"><span class="rnum">4</span><span class="rverdict">UNSTATED</span><span class="rtext">What the money could have earned instead<span class="rfind"><span class="bang">! </span><b>Supplied.</b> Frontier’s discount rate is undisclosed. The footnote that should name it reads “Error! Reference source not found.”</span></span></div></div><p class="foot">Read the map →</p></div>

  <p class="sizetag">Extension card, 26rem</p>
  <div class="card panel"><p class="eyebrow">The Whetstone · this question is mapped</p><p class="q">Is a nuclear pathway cheaper than a renewables-only one for Australia?</p><div class="poles"><span>← nuclear cheaper</span><span>renewables cheaper →</span></div><div class="beam"></div><div class="struts"><div class="strutcol" style="left:12.5%;transform:translateX(-50%)"><div class="strut unstated"></div></div><div class="strutcol" style="left:37.5%;transform:translateX(-50%)"><div class="strut contested"></div></div><div class="strutcol" style="left:62.5%;transform:translateX(-50%)"><div class="strut contested"></div></div><div class="strutcol" style="left:87.5%;transform:translateX(-50%)"><div class="strut unstated"></div></div></div><div class="baseline"></div><div class="words"><div class="wordcol" style="left:12.5%"><span class="word">UNSTATED</span><span class="ord">1</span></div><div class="wordcol" style="left:37.5%"><span class="word">CONTESTED</span><span class="ord">2</span></div><div class="wordcol" style="left:62.5%"><span class="word">CONTESTED</span><span class="ord">3</span></div><div class="wordcol" style="left:87.5%"><span class="word">UNSTATED</span><span class="ord">4</span></div></div><div class="rows"><div class="row"><span class="rnum">1</span><span class="rverdict">UNSTATED</span><span class="rtext">How often a reactor runs<span class="rfind"><span class="bang">! </span><b>Supplied.</b> Frontier needs 90 per cent uptime and never states it. GenCost prices 53 to 89 per cent, from coal’s own record.</span></span></div><div class="row"><span class="rnum">2</span><span class="rverdict">CONTESTED</span><span class="rtext">What the first plant costs<span class="rfind"><b>Factual.</b> Frontier removes the first-of-a-kind premium by the time nuclear is built. GenCost puts it above 100 per cent.</span></span></div><div class="row"><span class="rnum">3</span><span class="rverdict">CONTESTED</span><span class="rtext">How long the asset lives<span class