  <div class="card narrow"><p class="eyebrow">The Whetstone · this question is mapped</p><p class="q">Is a nuclear pathway cheaper than a renewables-only one for Australia?</p><div class="rows"><div class="row"><span class="rnum">1</span><span class="rverdict">UNSTATED</span><span class="rtext">How often a reactor runs<span class="rfind"><span class="bang">! </span><b>Supplied.</b> Frontier needs 90 per cent uptime and never states it. GenCost prices 53 to 89 per cent, from coal’s own record.</span></span></div><div class="row"><span class="rnum">2</span><span class="rverdict">CONTESTED</span><span class="rtext">What the first plant costs<span class="rfind"><b>Factual.</b> Frontier removes the first-of-a-kind premium by the time nuclear is built. GenCost puts it above 100 per cent.</span></span></div><div class="row"><span class="rnum">3</span><span class="rverdict">CONTESTED</span><span class="rtext">How long the asset lives<span class="rfind"><b>Judgment call.</b> The same build cost spread over 50 years or recovered over 30. The choice is never argued for on either side.</span></span></div><div class="row"><span class="rnum">4</span><span class="rverdict">UNSTATED</span><span class="rtext">What the money could have earned instead<span class="rfind"><span class="bang">! </span><b>Supplied.</b> Frontier’s discount rate is undisclosed. The footnote that should name it reads “Error! Reference source not found.”</span></span></div></div><p class="foot">Read the map →</p></div>

  <hr class="rule">
  <h2>C. The ledger</h2>
  <p class="verdictline">Diagram and text as one object, not two</p>
  <p class="note">A and B separate the picture from the words, so the eye has to travel between them and bind them by ordinal number. This puts a small gauge on each row instead: the same three terminations, drawn horizontally at the left of the line it describes. Nothing to bind, no numerals needed, and it degrades to B by deleting one column. It also has room to name both sides of a contested premise, which is what the briefing is actually about.</p>

  <p class="sizetag">Site width, 42rem</p>
  <div class="card site"><p class="eyebrow">The Whetstone · this question is mapped</p><p class="q">Is a nuclear pathway cheaper than a renewables-only one for Australia?</p><div class="poles"><span>← nuclear cheaper</span><span>renewables cheaper →</span></div><div class="beam"></div><div style="height:10px"></div><div class="lrow"><div class="gauge"><span class="bar"><span class="seg gap" style="width:54px"></span></span><span class="gword">UNSTATED</span></div><div><span class="rtext">How often a reactor runs</span><span class="rfind"><span class="bang">! </span><b>Supplied.</b> Frontier needs 90 per cent uptime and never states it. GenCost prices 53 to 89 per cent, from coal’s own record.</span><div class="cmp"><div class="side"><b>nuclear cheaper</b>90% of the time (never stated)</div><div class="side"><b>renewables cheaper</b>53 to 89%, coal’s best decade</div></div></div></div><div class="lrow"><div class="gauge"><span class="bar"><span class="seg" style="width:34px"></span><span class="seg miss" style="width:20px"></span></span><span class="gword">CONTESTED</span></div><div><span class="rtext">What the first plant costs</span><span class="rfind"><b>Factual.</b> Frontier removes the first-of-a-kind premium by the time nuclear is built. GenCost puts it above 100 per cent.</span><div class="cmp"><div class="side"><b>nuclear cheaper</b>premium removed</div><div class="side"><b>renewables cheaper</b>over 100% premium</div></div></div></div><div class="lrow"><div class="gauge"><span class="bar"><span class="seg" style="width:34px"></span><span class="seg miss" style="width:20px"></span></span><span class="gword">CONTESTED</span></div><div><span class="rtext">How long the asset lives</span><span class="rfind"><b>Judgment call.</b> The same build cost spread over 50 years or recovered over 30. The choice is never argued for on either side.</span><div class="cmp"><div class="side"><b>nuclear cheaper</b>spread over 50 years</div><div class="side"><b>renewables cheaper</b>recovered over 30 years</div></div></div></div><div class="lrow"><div class="gauge"><span class="bar"><span class="seg gap" style="width:54px"></span></span><span class="gword">UNSTATED</span></div><div><span class="rtext">What the money could have earned instead</span><span class="rfind"><span class="bang">! </span><b>Supplied.</b> Frontier’s discount rate is undisclosed. The footnote that should name it reads “Error! Reference source not found.”</span><div class="cmp"><div class="side"><b>nuclear cheaper</b>undisclosed</div><div class="side"><b>renewables cheaper</b>raised 6% to 7%, stated</div></div></div></div><p class="foot">Read the map →</p></div>

